From: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/of: -EPROBE_DEFER ONLY for the QUP streams (dace bring-up)

On dace apps-smmu is a module that cannot probe until qnoc-monaco registers the
ICC provider (initramfs load). Devices with "iommus" that probe earlier are
left without an IOMMU domain because of_iommu_xlate() returns the -ETIMEDOUT
from driver_deferred_probe_check_state() (modules load after the initcalls and
driver_deferred_probe_timeout==0) and of_iommu_configure() only respects
-EPROBE_DEFER.

And on this SoC being left without a domain is NOT harmless: the firmware leaves
apps-smmu with CLIENTPD=0 and USFCFG=1 (bit LOCKED by TZ: the read-back does not
change) -> unidentified streams are ABORTED. The firmware table only has 4 SMRs
(0xc0 eMMC, 0xa0/0x120 USB, 0x422 handoff), so:

  - eMMC, USB, qcrypto, tmc...: they are ALREADY in the firmware CB and work
    with physical addresses. If Linux attaches them to a domain it CHANGES
    their CB and the boot hangs (measured 2026-09-20 with the unconditional
    patch) -> they must be left as they were (-ETIMEDOUT, still no domain).
  - 0xe3 (qcom,qupv3_0_geni_se wrapper, which maps the SPI/UART buffers:
    geni_se_tx/rx_dma_prep -> dma_map_single(wrapper->dev)) and 0xf6 (slate
    GPI-DMA): they are NOT in the table -> their DMA is ABORTED (RX_SBE on the
    HS UART, "general error" 0x40 from the slate GSI/GPI -> crown and BT
    blocked). For them we DO need to wait for apps-smmu and give them a domain.

That is why -EPROBE_DEFER is limited to those two stream IDs.

The no-patch alternative (deferred_probe_timeout=N on the cmdline) was tried and
is NOT valid: it delays ALL dependencies and leaves the USB chain without a UDC.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
Signed-off-by: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/of_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/of_iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/of_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/of_iommu.c
@@ -39,8 +39,25 @@
 	 * IOMMU device we're waiting for, which will be useful if we ever get
 	 * a proper probe-ordering dependency mechanism in future.
 	 */
-	if (!ops)
+	if (!ops) {
+		/*
+		 * dace: -EPROBE_DEFER only for the QUP wrapper (0xe3) and GPI (0xf6).
+		 * The firmware leaves sCR0.USFCFG=1 (locked by TZ) and its SMR table
+		 * has no entry for these two, so their DMA with a physical address is
+		 * aborted. The other masters already have a firmware context bank and
+		 * must keep using it: attaching them to a Linux domain breaks them.
+		 */
+		u32 dace_sid = (iommu_spec->args_count > 0) ?
+				iommu_spec->args[0] : 0xffffffff;
+
+		if (dace_sid == 0xe3 || dace_sid == 0xf6) {
+			dev_err(dev,
+				"DACE-IOMMU: sid=0x%x -> -EPROBE_DEFER (waiting for apps-smmu)\n",
+				dace_sid);
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		}
 		return driver_deferred_probe_check_state(dev);
+	}
 
 	if (!try_module_get(ops->owner))
 		return -ENODEV;
